   ok    a measured step that writes nothing passes
   ok    a tool that wrote in-tree is refused
   ok    a gate step with no row is refused — an empty file must not read as proof
   ok    a missing measurement file is refused
   ok    a row with no measured list is refused
   ok    a step naming no python or node tool is not a hole
   ok    a row for a tool no longer gated is not a failure — it is stale, not wrong
   ok    a NEW self-test added without a measurement is refused, which is the point of this gate
   ok    a write git classified as ignored (a build product) passes
   ok    a write to a TRACKED path under site/ is refused, where the old `site/` prefix excused it
   ok    a row that was never classified is refused, not read as clean
   ok    a schema-1 measurement, from before classification, is refused — re-measure, not reinterpret
   ok    an `exempt` list, even with a reason, is refused — the hand-kept list does not grow back
   ok    an empty `exempt` map is not a list
   ok    the finding names the invocation that wrote, not just the tool
  self-test: every assertion fires when broken
